{
  "name": "task-163-m1-stitch-ab",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "artifact_dir": "reviews/task-163/001-m1-stitch-ab/artifacts",
  "description": "Task 163 M1 TC-039 A/B: ec_distann stitched (build_shards=4, closure_epsilon=0.1) vs monolithic (build_shards=1) at 10k/50k/100k, recall@10 + latency + storage, rabitq codec (D7 default). Exit bar: stitched recall within 0.001 of monolithic at equal search params (FR-077-AC-1). distinct_recall == recall for this AM: one global Vamana graph, one logical record per vector, no partition duplication (ADR-085), so recall@10 is the distinct_recall. Bespoke config (not the canonical lane sweep): the variant axis is build_shards (the M1 change), so both arms hold every other option at the profile default and differ only in shard count -- this isolates the stitch effect per the A/B-per-change rule. Per-arm table isolation via distinct prefixes. Sweep drives ec_distann.top_k (the D9 early-exit bar); hop_rounds stays the NFR-019 cap. Protocol: recall step precedes latency step per arm (task-168 first-point trap).",
  "defaults": {
    "pg": 18,
    "socket_dir": "/home/peter/.pgrx",
    "bits": 4,
    "seed": 42,
    "queries_limit": 200,
    "iterations": 200,
    "force_index": true,
    "sample_backend_memory": true,
    "memory_sample_interval_ms": 25
  },
